Preaching channels especially benefit from showing the breadth of scripture — congregants tune in expecting to encounter passages they don't already know by heart. Branch into less-frequently-preached passages: 2 Kings 6 (Elisha and the chariots of fire), Nehemiah 8 (the public reading of the law), Acts 17 (Paul at the Areopagus), Romans 9-11 (Israel's place in salvation history), Hebrews 11 (the hall of faith), Revelation 7 (the great multitude), Job 38-41 (the Lord answers from the whirlwind), Ezekiel 37 (the valley of dry bones), Hosea 11 (the father's heart).
